<title>UK: BSkyB gains after positive Merrill comment.</title>
<headline>BSkyB gains after positive Merrill comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Sky Broadcasting Plc rose on Wednesday after positive comment from Merrill Lynch, traders said.</p>
<p>Extending their rebound from the five-month low of 473p set December 13, BSkyB shares were up 14-1/2p at 533 by 1225 GMT in active trading of 3.2 million shares.</p>
<p>Sources said analyst Neil Blackley at Merrill had assumed coverage of the stock and had rated it &quot;accumulate&quot; with a price target of 560p.</p>
<p>Blackley was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
